      "side": 1,
      "message": "Especially if the quirk is set, I\u0027d also validate that PD_HEADER_CNT(head) \u003d\u003d (cnt-3).\n\nLater code would read garbage if RX_HDR is stale, for example if the TCPC gets a hard reset, resets BYTE_CNT to 0, but leaves stale data in RX_HDR.  This is the bug that I was fixing in the first place (until I realized that BYTE_CNT must include the header length).\n\nI imagine that, with current PS8751 FW, there is no way to distinguish between hard reset (invalid data) and data with length 0.",
      "revId": "d127b5c5493716cb6ff12fceb6c167f62ba5d9c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
